<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Poland</h1><p class="st-meta">960 CE – 1025 CE (approx.) · capital Gniezno</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Polish state, created by the Piast dukes around Gniezno, which adopted Christianity in 966 and became a kingdom in 1025.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 960 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-i">Mieszko I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a> ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polans-western">Polans</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-greater-poland">Greater Poland</a> from strongholds at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poznan">Poznan</a>. He married the Bohemian princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doubravka-of-bohemia">Dubrawka</a> and was baptised in 966, bringing his realm into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Christendom</a>. By the 990s he had added <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Pomerania</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesser-poland">Lesser Poland</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast</a> dukes ruled through a network of fortified centres and a mounted retinue, and supported themselves with tribute and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. Around 991 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-i">Mieszko</a> placed his lands under papal protection in the document known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagome-iudex">Dagome iudex</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Boleslaw I</a> welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Otto III</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-gniezno">Congress of Gniezno</a> in 1000, which created an archbishopric at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Boleslaw I</a> fought the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry II</a> for years, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen">Peace of Bautzen</a> in 1018, and the same year briefly took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>. Shortly before his death in 1025 he was crowned king, and the duchy became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1025-1385">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1025-1385).</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-poland.jpg" alt="Duchy of Poland" width="320" height="225"><figcaption>Image: Elevatorrailfan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Civitas_Schinesghe_1000.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>960 CE – 1025 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gniezno</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mieszko I, Boleslaw I the Brave</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Civitas Schinesghe, Piast Poland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=992&amp;focus=duchy-of-poland" aria-label="Duchy of Poland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5075 366 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Poland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5395 622L5457 692M5395 622L5229 694M5395 622L5457 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5457 692h0M5229 694h0M5457 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5395 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5395 622h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>